---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Auspicious Music in English — Event planning and strings"
  description="The English entry to the Auspicious Music event-music planner and selected technical guides about strings, recording and music production."
  canonicalPath="/en/"
  lang="en"
  alternatePath="/"
  headerOverDark={true}
>
  <Fragment slot="head"><style is:global>
    @layer components {
      .en-hero { background: var(--stage); color: var(--stage-text); padding-block: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 8rem); }
      .en-hero .kicker, .en-hero .lede { color: var(--stage-muted); }
      .en-hero h1 { max-width: 15ch; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
      .en-hero .lede { max-width: 58ch; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
      .en-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .75rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
      .en-grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
      @media (min-width: 780px) { .en-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
      .en-card { display: grid; align-content: start; min-height: 13rem; padding: 1.4rem; text-decoration: none; }
      .en-card h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; }
      .en-card p { margin-top: .65rem; color: var(--muted); }
      .en-card span { margin-top: auto; padding-top: 1.5rem; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 650; }
      .en-note { max-width: 64rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--ember-bright); padding-left: 1.25rem; }
    }
  </style></Fragment>
  <main id="content">
    <section class="en-hero">
      <div class="shell">
        <p class="kicker">English at Auspicious Music</p>
        <h1>Plan the music. Understand the string decision.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Auspicious Music is primarily published in German. This page gives English-speaking visitors a clear route to the bilingual event-music planner and to a selected technical library about recording, production and sound design.</p>
        <div class="en-actions"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="/en/tools/event-music-planner/">Open the event-music planner</a><a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/resources/">Browse the technical library</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="band sheet-lift">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head"><div><p class="kicker">Choose a route</p><h2>English content with a defined purpose</h2></div><p>These are curated English routes, not machine-translated copies of every German page.</p></div>
        <div class="en-grid">
          <a class="card en-card" href="/en/tools/event-music-planner/"><h2>Event-music planner</h2><p>Turn an occasion, musical moments, setting and practical limits into a reviewable brief. Entries stay in your browser.</p><span>Create a plan →</span></a>
          <a class="card en-card" href="/recording/"><h2>Viola recording</h2><p>The recording hub is currently German-first. Its practical structure covers room, placement and repeatable session decisions.</p><span>Open the German hub →</span></a>
          <a class="card en-card" href="/resources/"><h2>Technical library</h2><p>English guides and browser tools for music production, sampled instruments, recording and music for media.</p><span>Explore resources →</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="band band-surface"><div class="shell en-note"><h2>Who is behind the current publication?</h2><p style="margin-top:.75rem">Matthias Ramahi is the current publisher. Violist Kim-Marie Borger is the named current musical expert for the German-first viola, repertoire and event-planning area. Her own website remains the authoritative source for current performances, offers and availability. The present publication is independent from the domain's former operator and does not claim the former catalogue or its rights.</p></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
